From: Noltbook Phase 1 deployment
Subject: [PATCH] rtpconn: guard against nil c.group in pushClientAction

handleAction dereferences c.group without a nil check when handling
pushClientAction. A client that has just left a group sets c.group to
nil (webclient.go:1341), but a pushClientAction queued before that may
still be pending in its action channel. Dequeuing it then panics on
c.group.Name().

There is no recover() in the package, so this panic terminates the
whole process, dropping every group on the server rather than the one
connection involved.

The same handler already uses this exact idiom at webclient.go:1402:
    if c.group == nil || c.group.Name() != m.Group {

--- a/rtpconn/webclient.go
+++ b/rtpconn/webclient.go
@@ -1160,7 +1160,7 @@
 		}
 
 	case pushClientAction:
-		if a.group != c.group.Name() {
+		if c.group == nil || a.group != c.group.Name() {
 			log.Printf("got client for wrong group")
 			return nil
 		}
